  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Atomics Aeronautical Systems has $1.2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems won 126 awards so far, with an average award size of $9.6M. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligations are down 26.5% year over year. Historical obligations show a peak at $2.3B in FY24 and a low of $1.6B in FY25, with prior years at $2B in FY21, $1.9B in FY22, and $1.8B in FY23. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer of General Atomics Aeronautical Systems with $895M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $314M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for General Atomics Aeronautical Systems at $404M, followed by Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $315M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $228M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligations changed year over year?",
        "body": "General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligations are down 26.5% year over year. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligations have moved from $2B in FY21, $1.9B in FY22, $1.8B in FY23, $2.3B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, to $1.2B in FY26. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems current-year total is a fiscal year to date partial figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets does General Atomics Aeronautical Systems serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer of General Atomics Aeronautical Systems with $895M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $314M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for General Atomics Aeronautical Systems at $404M, Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is $315M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is $228M. Additional markets include Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $148M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $68.8M."
      }
    ]
